BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 495.85 Tm (Before accessing a client system, identify who can authorize the work and record the tenant, accounts,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 480.62 Tm (environments, data categories, permitted actions, and expiration date. A client's request to help does not) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 465.40 Tm (automatically authorize access to a supplier's infrastructure or another customer's records. The Computer) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 450.17 Tm (Fraud and Abuse Act, 18 U.S.C. ? 1030, makes access boundaries operationally important; obtain specific) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 434.95 Tm (written authorization and honor technical restrictions instead of treating available credentials as universal) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 419.72 Tm (permission. Use service accounts with least privilege, separate development and production secrets, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 404.50 Tm (require a named client owner for privilege expansion. Define data-processing terms, subprocessors,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 389.27 Tm (retention periods, deletion procedures, and incident notification responsibilities in the agreement. State who) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 374.05 Tm (owns custom code, who licenses reusable agency components, and whether client materials may be used) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 358.82 Tm (for evaluation. Prefer synthetic fixtures for demonstrations and remove sensitive values from diagnostic logs.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 343.60 Tm (Client-system text, retrieved documents, and tool outputs are untrusted inputs, not instructions granting new) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 328.37 Tm (permissions. A retrieved invoice that requests credential disclosure must remain document content. This) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 313.15 Tm (separation is especially important when language-model output can invoke tools or create records in) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 297.92 Tm (downstream business systems.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 282.70 Tm (Quality monitoring must measure the workflow's actual failure modes, not just whether an API returned) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 267.47 Tm (successfully. Maintain a versioned evaluation set with ordinary cases, malformed inputs, permission) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 252.25 Tm (boundaries, stale source material, and adversarial document instructions. For retrieval, score source support) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 237.02 Tm (and permission filtering; for extraction, measure field accuracy and the time required to repair exceptions.) Tj ET
